Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1D-MATH-CDF", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996335738629848*^9, 3.9963357454370737`*^9}, 
   3.996672469810019*^9, {3.996753015752389*^9, 3.996753019402701*^9}, 
   3.996753731910015*^9, {3.997449759368969*^9, 3.997449759880464*^9}, {
   3.997459139681313*^9, 3.9974591417827387`*^9}, 3.9974604823561*^9, {
   3.99747641984694*^9, 
   3.997476420139122*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1efddb00-d56d-4360-98e0-\
c6d487b0b2d5"],

Cell["\<\
The 1D-MATH-CDF test suite verifies the mathematical properties and \
functional forms of the cumulative distribution functions (CDFs) across \
position, momentum, and energy spaces. The suite confirms that these \
functions satisfy strict asymptotic boundary conditions, ensuring they \
correctly bound the cumulative probability between zero and one at the \
respective spatial and energy limits. Furthermore, it validates the \
Fundamental Theorem of Calculus by proving that the explicit analytical \
derivatives of the CDFs perfectly recover their corresponding probability \
density functions. Finally, the tests evaluate the interval probability \
functions to guarantee exact unit normalization when integrated over the full \
physical domains.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.996755904602223*^9, {3.9974615170631638`*^9, 
   3.997461519208111*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e7e3474f-8b31-47b8-b385-\
afe7c4c91d5b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

